(1) P2TP2A organizes women's protection services.
(2) Women's protection services by P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) involve elements of:
   a. health;
   b. psychology;
   c. law;
   d. religious leaders;
   e. social; and
   f. economic.
(3) Further provisions regarding the establishment, membership composition, duties, and functions of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be stipulated by Regent's Decree.

Article 14
Implementation of protection for women is provided to: a. women workers/laborers;
b. elderly women;
c. women with disabilities;
d. homeless women;
e. domestic women workers;
f. women as family economic supporters;
g. women former inmates of correctional institutions;
h. women victims of disasters;
i. women commercial sex workers; and
j. women victims of violence.

Article 3
Every Woman with disability has the right to obtain:
a. education in all units, pathways, types and levels of education;
b. work and decent livelihood in accordance with the type and degree of disability, education and ability;
c. equal treatment to play a role in development and enjoy its results;
d. accessibility for the purpose of her independence;
e. rehabilitation, social assistance and maintenance of social welfare standards; and
f. equal rights to develop talents, abilities and social life.

